  "summary": "Astal is Sega's side-scrolling platform adventure, first released for Saturn in Japan on 28 April 1995.",
  "body": [
    "Astal is Sega's side-scrolling platform adventure, first released for Saturn in Japan on 28 April 1995. Its story takes place on Quartalia, a world created from a jewel, where Astal was made to protect Leda. Their separation sends him across brightly coloured landscapes to find her. Hand-drawn graphics give the world a storybook appearance, supported by animated sequences produced by Tokyo Movie Shinsha. The visual detail makes the setting an important part of the journey, while Astal's strength lets him interact with its objects in unusually direct ways.",
    "Astal can strike and throw enemies, punch the ground to stun nearby opponents and charge a powerful breath that blows obstacles away. Trees and rocks can also be lifted and thrown. These actions make the landscape a source of practical tools, with a large object becoming something to use rather than simply pass. Running and jumping still carry him across gaps, but encounters often ask which form of strength fits the situation. A group nearby may be easier to stun with a ground strike than meet one opponent at a time.",
    "A bird companion adds another layer to the action. Defeating special glowing enemies fills a meter that allows Astal to call on the bird's help, while a second player can take control of its attacks in an asymmetrical cooperative mode. The two characters therefore contribute in different ways to the same stage. Tatsuyuki Maeda and Tatsuya Kousaki composed the music. Alongside the hand-drawn environments, the companion and Astal's exaggerated physical actions give the adventure the quality of an animated tale whose scenery can be touched, lifted and thrown."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "A world made from a jewel",
    "Strength in the scenery",
    "A bird beside the journey"
  ],
